1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,033
<i>Kang Dae Hyun,
you are under arrest!</i>

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:03,000
<i>Please do not arrest him!
He did nothing wrong!</i>

3
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:04,067
<i>Just listen to your father,
okay?</i>

4
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,333
<i>When I say I will get revenge,
I mean it!</i>

5
00:00:07,467 --> 00:00:09,700
<i>I strongly feel that he is not
the only target.</i>

6
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:10,967
<i> But all of us are.</i>

7
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,000
<i> I will not stop until
that criminal syndicate is gone.</i>

8
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:16,133
<i>If I were the leader
of that syndicate,</i>

9
00:00:16,267 --> 00:00:17,967
<i>I would probably
have you killed as well!</i>

10
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,833
<i>Tell me where the syndicate
is hiding.</i>

11
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:21,833
<i> I don't know.</i>

12
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:23,033
<i> My child trusts you deeply.</i>

13
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:24,533
<i>I hope you do not break
that trust.</i>

14
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,567
<i>He cannot stay here
at the precinct.</i>

15
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,467
<i>But do not worry,
you are not alone here.</i>

16
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,433
<i> I am so happy to see you.</i>

17
00:00:32,367 --> 00:00:34,633
<i> [OPENING THEME MUSIC]</i>

18
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:50,500
Why are they here?

19
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,467
Why? Do you not want them here?

20
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,233
I did not say that.

21
00:00:55,367 --> 00:00:57,900
But the syndicate is after me.

22
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:00,333
Everyone is already involved.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

23
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:01,633
This is the only thing I can do

24
00:01:01,767 --> 00:01:03,900
to protect all of you.

25
00:01:05,633 --> 00:01:09,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

26
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,400
<i> Are you sure you trust Jin Ho?</i>

27
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:14,800
<i> What about you?</i>

28
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,367
<i> Yes, Sir, I do.</i>

29
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:19,900
<i> Me...</i>

30
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:21,300
<i> I am not sure.</i>

31
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:27,167
<i> If I keep you with me,</i>

32
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,000
<i> I can protect you better.</i>

33
00:01:29,133 --> 00:01:30,600
<i> What do you mean, Dad?</i>

34
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:32,667
<i> All we know is that...</i>

35
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,800
<i>you could be targets
of the syndicate.</i>

36
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:36,033
<i> The three of you</i>

37
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:39,467
<i>need to be placed in a safe
location with Jin Ho.</i>

38
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,533
<i> That is it.</i>

39
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:44,033
<i> Wait, Miguel.</i>

40
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:46,467
<i> Are you sure about this plan?</i>

41
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,067
<i> Clarissa, this is the only way</i>

42
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,900
<i> I can keep an eye on them.</i>

43
00:01:53,133 --> 00:01:55,633
<i>Let us also use this opportunity</i>

44
00:01:55,767 --> 00:01:56,933
<i> to make Jin Ho confess</i>

45
00:01:57,067 --> 00:01:59,467
<i> about these syndicates.</i>

46
00:02:01,367 --> 00:02:03,933
<i>You said yourselves
that you are close to him.</i>

47
00:02:04,067 --> 00:02:05,433
<i> Make him confess.</i>

48
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:07,967
<i> Can you help me?</i>

49
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,667
We will stay here for now

50
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,833
while the situation is intense.

51
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:17,367
At least I can be
with my friends.

52
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,233
At least we are together.

53
00:02:19,367 --> 00:02:20,767
That is solid, right?

54
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:22,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,733
This is not a vacation,
you might be forgetting.

56
00:02:24,867 --> 00:02:28,000
We are here to hide
from the syndicates.

57
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:30,533
And you cannot do anything

58
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:33,300
without telling me first.

59
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:39,367
Andrew, no one will be
babysitting you here.

60
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:41,500
So, while we are
in this safe house,

61
00:02:41,633 --> 00:02:43,633
we work together.

62
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:46,267
Also...

63
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,200
no cell phones,

64
00:02:48,367 --> 00:02:51,467
internet, Wi Fi, or computers.

65
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,633
The enemies might trace us.

66
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:55,467
But why...

67
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,400
do you have a cell phone?

68
00:02:57,533 --> 00:02:58,500
This?

69
00:02:58,633 --> 00:02:59,667
That is not personal.

70
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,533
It is a burner phone,
only for calling the office.

71
00:03:05,667 --> 00:03:09,867
I am sure the syndicate...

72
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,967
is doing everything to find you.

73
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:16,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:03:21,567 --> 00:03:22,500
Oh, this is ours.

75
00:03:22,633 --> 00:03:24,067
Thank you, Aunt Clarissa.

76
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,500
You are welcome.

77
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:26,833
Here.

78
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:31,633
Where is Joey?

79
00:03:31,767 --> 00:03:33,033
Ah...

80
00:03:33,167 --> 00:03:35,500
she is, on a vacation.

81
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:36,833
Ah...

82
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:38,467
who is she with?

83
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,367
Uncle Miguel?

84
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,033
Amazing, right?
Uncle came back to life.

85
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,967
You really are something,
that is a long story.

86
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:49,967
You might not still get it.

87
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:54,267
But, Joey is on vacation
with her friends.

88
00:03:55,367 --> 00:03:56,633
Do you need anything from her?

89
00:03:56,767 --> 00:03:57,767
I might be of help.

90
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,300
Nothing, Aunt Clarissa.

91
00:03:59,433 --> 00:04:00,967
I just miss Joey.

92
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,467
- Oh...
- Goodbye!

93
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,000
Bye. Take care, okay?

94
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:05,400
Yes!

95
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:26,833
- Ma'am!
- Is Joey home?

96
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,167
No. She is on a vacation.

97
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,533
Only Aunt Clarissa is there,

98
00:04:30,667 --> 00:04:31,667
together with two police
officers.

99
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:32,767
Do you want me to call her?

100
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,500
Oh, no, never mind.

101
00:04:34,633 --> 00:04:36,267
You know...

102
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:41,500
Here take this, buy some snacks.

103
00:04:41,633 --> 00:04:43,400
Just keep this between us.

104
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,300
- Thank you!
- You may go now.

105
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:53,000
Where could you be hiding, Joey?

106
00:04:57,033 --> 00:04:58,233
All right, thank you!

107
00:04:58,367 --> 00:04:59,467
Go back to your posts now.

108
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,867
- Yes, Sir.
- Okay.

109
00:05:04,667 --> 00:05:05,667
Oh...

110
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,000
This is a lot, Dad.

111
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:10,100
They might have a big appetite.

112
00:05:11,467 --> 00:05:13,133
[COUGHS]

113
00:05:13,267 --> 00:05:14,700
Oh, Joey, are you okay?

114
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:16,700
Ah...

115
00:05:16,833 --> 00:05:19,400
I am just not feeling very well.

116
00:05:19,533 --> 00:05:21,733
- [CLEARS THROAT]
- All right, after you eat

117
00:05:21,867 --> 00:05:24,100
- take your medicine, okay?
- Yes.

118
00:05:24,233 --> 00:05:25,700
What do you want me to cook?

119
00:05:25,833 --> 00:05:29,033
Anything is fine, when you cook,
it always tastes good.

120
00:05:29,167 --> 00:05:30,167
Then I will do the cooking.

121
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,500
I will be the one
to prepare lunch.

122
00:05:31,633 --> 00:05:33,467
I will do it.
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,633
Wow, you?

124
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,667
You are going to cook?

125
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,367
Do you not always eat
at restaurants?

126
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,133
- That's it.
- Why would you cook?

127
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:41,467
Then that means
I have better taste than you.

128
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,233
Maybe all you know how to cook

129
00:05:43,367 --> 00:05:45,700
are hotdogs, rice, and eggs.

130
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:47,667
Joey, just sit there.

131
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,800
I will give you the best lunch.

132
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,867
All right,
the three of you cook then.

133
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,100
I will stay with Joey for now,
okay?

134
00:05:57,067 --> 00:05:58,267
Okay?

135
00:06:00,567 --> 00:06:01,933
[RUSTLING AND RATTLING]

136
00:06:02,067 --> 00:06:03,300
I will get that.

137
00:06:03,433 --> 00:06:05,667
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

138
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:09,767
[ENERGIZING MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:24,767
Okay.

140
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:28,867
[ENERGIZING MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:44,333
[SIZZLING]

142
00:06:45,167 --> 00:06:46,567
Oh, Jin Ho...

143
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:48,333
did you get my instructions,

144
00:06:48,467 --> 00:06:49,800
or do you want me
to explain in English?

145
00:06:49,933 --> 00:06:50,933
No problem.

146
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:53,600
Thanks for teaching me,
Major Delgado.

147
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:55,567
All right. If you need anything,

148
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:57,133
just let me know, okay?

149
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,500
I know what you are doing.

150
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:03,533
It's obvious.

151
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:05,367
I'm just cooking chicken adobo.

152
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,633
[SCOFFS]

153
00:07:06,767 --> 00:07:08,300
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:07:08,433 --> 00:07:10,700
You are just trying to suck up
to Major Miguel Delgado

155
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:12,733
for Joey.

156
00:07:12,867 --> 00:07:14,900
[SCOFFS]

157
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:17,400
Seems like ostrich to me.

158
00:07:17,533 --> 00:07:20,200
So big, so many.

159
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:22,333
I am just following the recipe.

160
00:07:22,467 --> 00:07:24,367
And you know...

161
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:25,900
Joey is going to love this

162
00:07:26,033 --> 00:07:29,600
because it will taste
like her father's dish.

163
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:31,000
What are you cooking anyway?

164
00:07:31,133 --> 00:07:32,533
What?

165
00:07:34,233 --> 00:07:35,267
Secret.

166
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,700
What the heck is that?

167
00:07:37,833 --> 00:07:39,233
It is gross.
Look.

168
00:07:39,367 --> 00:07:41,267
Look, you smell.

169
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,533
So good.

170
00:07:42,667 --> 00:07:44,667
Bad, bad.
I will show you mine.

171
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,733
Say what you want to say.

172
00:07:45,867 --> 00:07:48,267
I am sure you are going
to embarrass yourself.

173
00:07:48,433 --> 00:07:51,033
No, it is really delicious
chicken adobo.

174
00:07:51,167 --> 00:07:52,167
- I'll show you.
- No, no.

175
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:55,233
This is, "Saranghae."

176
00:07:55,367 --> 00:07:56,167
- "Saranghae?"
- Yes.

177
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:57,733
- It means I love you.
- "Keopta."

178
00:07:57,867 --> 00:08:00,133
"Keopta."

179
00:08:00,267 --> 00:08:03,167
[SIZZLING]

180
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:07,500
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

181
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,367
Hey.

182
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,200
So you are still a kid.

183
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:18,633
<i> She is already grown up.</i>

184
00:08:18,767 --> 00:08:20,900
<i>She can handle herself,
unlike you.</i>

185
00:08:21,067 --> 00:08:22,433
<i>You are still young.
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

186
00:08:22,567 --> 00:08:23,967
Once you taste my cooking,

187
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,067
you might say I am ready
to get married.

188
00:08:33,067 --> 00:08:36,467
You will definitely fall in love
with what I cook for you, Joey.

189
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,233
[CHUCKLES]

190
00:08:38,367 --> 00:08:39,733
Oh...

191
00:08:41,667 --> 00:08:44,000
Hon, after I finalize the venue

192
00:08:44,133 --> 00:08:47,000
for the foundation's
fundraising event,

193
00:08:47,133 --> 00:08:48,900
I will go visit Mom, okay?

194
00:08:49,033 --> 00:08:50,167
- All right.
- The investigation continues

195
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,267
- I might follow later.
- into the drug laboratory

196
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:55,600
<i> recently raided by the police.</i>

197
00:08:55,767 --> 00:08:56,933
<i> According to authorities,</i>

198
00:08:57,067 --> 00:08:59,100
<i> the wanted woman Liza De Leon</i>

199
00:08:59,233 --> 00:09:01,200
<i>may be involved.
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

200
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:03,467
<i> Anyone who has seen or knows</i>

201
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,367
<i>the whereabouts of Liza De Leon</i>

202
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:09,600
<i>is asked to call the number
shown on your screen.</i>

203
00:09:09,733 --> 00:09:11,200
<i> One possible syndicate member</i>

204
00:09:11,333 --> 00:09:14,000
<i> is now in our custody,</i>

205
00:09:14,133 --> 00:09:16,300
<i> and we hope he will help us</i>

206
00:09:16,433 --> 00:09:18,900
<i>identify and understand
their operation.</i>

207
00:09:19,033 --> 00:09:22,133
<i>We are hopeful
that we will succeed</i>

208
00:09:22,267 --> 00:09:25,667
<i> in capturing these criminals.</i>

209
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:29,633
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

210
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:37,700
[CAR REVVING]

211
00:09:37,833 --> 00:09:41,800
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:48,100
Are you okay, Hon?

213
00:09:48,233 --> 00:09:50,067
You seem affected...

214
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,033
by the news.

215
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:53,500
Huh?

216
00:09:53,633 --> 00:09:55,100
That's absurd.

217
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:57,433
Do not talk like that.

218
00:09:57,567 --> 00:10:01,200
Someone might get the wrong idea
about me if they hear you.

219
00:10:01,367 --> 00:10:04,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:10:04,433 --> 00:10:05,767
[DOOR SHUTS]

221
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,533
Why is he like that?

222
00:10:10,667 --> 00:10:14,800
He loses his temper so quickly.

223
00:10:15,333 --> 00:10:17,800
My cooking smells so good.

224
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,133
Do whatever you want.

225
00:10:19,267 --> 00:10:21,133
I am going ahead.
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

226
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:22,100
Try this!

227
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:24,367
It is really delicious,
very Filipino,

228
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:28,267
grilled with a touch of
American.

229
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,633
What American?

230
00:10:30,767 --> 00:10:31,900
There, American.

231
00:10:32,033 --> 00:10:34,567
Oh, that is impressive,
you really look like an expert.

232
00:10:34,733 --> 00:10:35,600
Of course.

233
00:10:35,733 --> 00:10:38,067
But why does it look kind of
burnt?

234
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,033
That can be covered here.

235
00:10:40,167 --> 00:10:41,100
There, see?

236
00:10:41,233 --> 00:10:42,900
It is not burnt anymore.

237
00:10:43,033 --> 00:10:44,167
Right? Boom.

238
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:46,633
Okay, thank you.

239
00:10:48,467 --> 00:10:50,433
Let us taste it, okay?

240
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:52,300
- It feels kind of tough.
- Huh?

241
00:10:53,933 --> 00:10:55,200
Oh!

242
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,600
It is okay, but it really
is a bit burnt.

243
00:10:59,733 --> 00:11:01,233
- But it has American.
- Yes.

244
00:11:01,367 --> 00:11:02,367
Mmm...

245
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,667
- Right?
- That's right.

246
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:06,300
Joey, try this adobo.

247
00:11:06,433 --> 00:11:08,533
Your father told me
how to cook this.

248
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:09,900
Yes.

249
00:11:10,033 --> 00:11:11,833
It is really delicious.

250
00:11:11,967 --> 00:11:13,100
Try it.

251
00:11:13,233 --> 00:11:17,500
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:11:19,067 --> 00:11:20,267
Jin Ho, congratulations!

253
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:21,700
Very good, very good!

254
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:22,900
Thank you.

255
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:24,667
He really got it right, right?
It is delicious.

256
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,367
Mmm...

257
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:27,467
Is it good?

258
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,667
It is good.

259
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,567
Just a bit salty compared to...

260
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,800
But it is good, right?

261
00:11:32,933 --> 00:11:35,000
And this is what I cooked
for you.

262
00:11:37,133 --> 00:11:40,300
Because the seasoning
is just right.

263
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:43,200
These two are salty
and a bit burnt.

264
00:11:43,367 --> 00:11:45,267
This one is just right.

265
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:47,733
- Macaroni soup?
- Macaroni soup, yes.

266
00:11:48,633 --> 00:11:52,433
Because I thought
that since Joey is sick,

267
00:11:52,567 --> 00:11:55,400
she needs to eat soup.

268
00:11:55,533 --> 00:11:57,233
Just being thoughtful.

269
00:11:57,367 --> 00:11:58,667
Okay.

270
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,433
Joey, here.

271
00:12:00,567 --> 00:12:01,967
Thank you.

272
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,867
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,500
Thank you.

274
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,433
Thank you.

275
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:14,700
You are welcome,
I really just want you

276
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:16,933
to feel better.

277
00:12:18,667 --> 00:12:22,400
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:23,733
But wait.

279
00:12:23,867 --> 00:12:27,167
Joey, my adobo is the best,
right?

280
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:29,533
Mine is also good.

281
00:12:29,667 --> 00:12:32,033
It is just slightly burnt.

282
00:12:32,167 --> 00:12:33,300
Just a little, right?

283
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:34,733
There is still more anyway.

284
00:12:34,867 --> 00:12:37,433
Well, everything is good.

285
00:12:37,567 --> 00:12:40,167
So, which one is the best?

286
00:12:41,867 --> 00:12:43,533
- The best?
- Yes.

287
00:12:44,167 --> 00:12:47,633
For me, the most
delicious one is...

288
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:50,933
[MIMICS DRUMROLL]

289
00:12:52,367 --> 00:12:53,867
Jin Ho's!

290
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Your adobo passed.

291
00:12:55,133 --> 00:12:56,800
Congratulations, okay?

292
00:12:56,933 --> 00:12:59,367
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,767
I will get back at you.

294
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,300
Do not bother,
it might burn again.

295
00:13:05,567 --> 00:13:07,533
Sir, if you can teach me more,

296
00:13:07,667 --> 00:13:10,067
I am willing to learn more
from you.

297
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:12,900
-[ANDREW CHUCKLES SARCASTICALLY]
-Okay, all right.

298
00:13:13,033 --> 00:13:15,033
You are really a suck-up, huh?

299
00:13:15,167 --> 00:13:16,167
What did you say?

300
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:18,033
- Suck-up.
- Suck-up?

301
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:19,733
You!

302
00:13:19,867 --> 00:13:21,167
Peter, Andrew, if you want,

303
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:24,567
I can share Major Delgado's
recipe with you.

304
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,500
Sure.

305
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:32,800
For me, this is what I like.

306
00:13:32,933 --> 00:13:34,167
Thank you for thinking about me

307
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:36,200
because I am not feeling well.

308
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:40,000
You are welcome. Enjoy.

309
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:43,333
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

310
00:13:50,533 --> 00:13:54,533
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:14:08,367 --> 00:14:10,233
Nothing.
We lost.

312
00:14:10,367 --> 00:14:11,833
What do you mean?

313
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:14,100
Our supplier backed out,

314
00:14:14,233 --> 00:14:16,533
and it looks like the one in the
South wants to back out too.

315
00:14:16,667 --> 00:14:18,200
Everyone knows
we are under pressure,

316
00:14:18,333 --> 00:14:20,933
so they are pulling away
from us.

317
00:14:21,067 --> 00:14:22,767
We will recover.

318
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,833
But before we do that...

319
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:28,867
the pests in our organization
must be eliminated.

320
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:31,367
Who are you referring to,
Berdugo?

321
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:32,900
Jin Ho?

322
00:14:33,033 --> 00:14:34,933
Delgado?

323
00:14:35,067 --> 00:14:36,300
Or Liza?

324
00:14:36,433 --> 00:14:37,700
All of them!

325
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:39,867
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:14:49,767 --> 00:14:50,667
Chief, it is a good thing

327
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,767
what happened already
made the news.

328
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:55,867
Instead of us being hunted,

329
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
many people are now
looking for them.

330
00:14:58,133 --> 00:15:00,433
<i> That was really the plan.</i>

331
00:15:00,567 --> 00:15:02,600
<i>How are things there?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

332
00:15:02,767 --> 00:15:04,167
Any updates?

333
00:15:05,667 --> 00:15:08,100
Not yet, but I will
find a way, Sir.

334
00:15:08,233 --> 00:15:09,767
<i> Just move fast, Major Delgado.</i>

335
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,033
<i> The longer this takes,</i>

336
00:15:11,167 --> 00:15:12,600
<i> the lower our chances</i>

337
00:15:12,733 --> 00:15:14,200
<i> of catching Berdugo become.</i>

338
00:15:14,333 --> 00:15:15,533
Yes, Chief.

339
00:15:15,667 --> 00:15:19,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

340
00:15:25,233 --> 00:15:26,633
Joey...

341
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:29,367
we need to talk to Jin Ho now.

342
00:15:32,867 --> 00:15:34,800
Okay, Dad.

343
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:39,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:15:47,633 --> 00:15:50,400
<i>The pests in our organization
must be eliminated.</i>

345
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:51,867
<i>Who are you referring to,
Berdugo?</i>

346
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,600
<i> Jin Ho? Delgado?</i>

347
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:54,633
<i> Or Liza?</i>

348
00:15:54,767 --> 00:15:56,167
<i> All of them!</i>

349
00:15:56,300 --> 00:16:00,333
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:16:00,467 --> 00:16:02,433
But what can we even do here?

351
00:16:02,567 --> 00:16:04,600
It is getting boring already.

352
00:16:04,733 --> 00:16:07,033
Do you want to walk around
for a bit?

353
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:08,800
Let's go?

354
00:16:08,967 --> 00:16:11,767
You really are always thinking
about going out.

355
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:14,233
Joey, it would be better
if you rest for now.

356
00:16:14,367 --> 00:16:17,867
Then think later about
what is okay to do, right?

357
00:16:19,467 --> 00:16:21,100
Andrew is right.

358
00:16:21,233 --> 00:16:22,300
Rest first.

359
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:24,400
You are not feeling well.

360
00:16:24,533 --> 00:16:27,267
And you, rest as well for now.

361
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,567
I will talk to the police
outside first.

362
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:30,800
This will just be quick, okay?

363
00:16:30,933 --> 00:16:31,767
Okay.

364
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:33,233
All right.

365
00:16:33,767 --> 00:16:35,967
Let us go upstairs.

366
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:38,800
Go ahead.
I will go to the restroom.

367
00:16:38,933 --> 00:16:40,700
Okay.

368
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:44,767
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:17:04,667 --> 00:17:08,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

370
00:17:12,833 --> 00:17:13,867
How is it here?

371
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,333
It is quiet, Sir.

372
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:16,700
It looks like no one even knows

373
00:17:16,833 --> 00:17:18,367
there is a house in this area.

374
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:22,700
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

375
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:41,867
[PHONE RINGING]

376
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:48,200
You have the nerve to call me!

377
00:17:48,367 --> 00:17:49,400
Liza...

378
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:52,967
I trusted you
and you betrayed me!

379
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:54,967
You are calling like
nothing happened?

380
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:55,800
<i> Liza...</i>

381
00:17:55,933 --> 00:17:57,400
Listen to me.

382
00:17:57,533 --> 00:17:58,767
Why?

383
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:00,533
Do you need my help?

384
00:18:00,667 --> 00:18:02,433
You are the one who needs help.

385
00:18:02,567 --> 00:18:04,633
Me? Really?

386
00:18:04,767 --> 00:18:06,400
<i> I need help?</i>

387
00:18:06,533 --> 00:18:08,100
Why do I need help?

388
00:18:08,233 --> 00:18:10,867
Because you know
your life is in danger.

389
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,833
I am sure that Berdugo
lost a lot from the raid,

390
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:16,267
and I am sure
that he blames you for it.

391
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:19,533
[SIGHS]

392
00:18:19,667 --> 00:18:21,767
Liza, listen.

393
00:18:22,733 --> 00:18:24,833
You know Berdugo
better than I do.

394
00:18:24,967 --> 00:18:26,700
<i> I'm sure that...</i>

395
00:18:26,833 --> 00:18:30,033
he will punish you
for what happened.

396
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,600
Do not be too complacent.

397
00:18:35,733 --> 00:18:37,600
Stay alert.

398
00:18:37,733 --> 00:18:38,933
All right, let us go back
to our posts.

399
00:18:39,067 --> 00:18:40,600
Copy, Sir.

400
00:18:40,733 --> 00:18:42,467
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

401
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,000
Go to the police, Liza.

402
00:18:45,133 --> 00:18:47,500
I will try to make a deal with
them.

403
00:18:47,633 --> 00:18:49,433
Until I know that you are safe,

404
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:51,100
<i> I won't talk.</i>

405
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,000
Think about it, Liza...

406
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:56,833
<i> and think fast.</i>

407
00:18:56,967 --> 00:19:00,067
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

408
00:19:02,633 --> 00:19:04,433
Jin Ho!

409
00:19:04,567 --> 00:19:05,900
What are you doing?

410
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:09,300
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

411
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:10,900
I got thirsty.

412
00:19:11,033 --> 00:19:15,067
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

413
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:18,233
Oh, all right,
go get some rest now.

414
00:19:18,367 --> 00:19:22,600
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

415
00:19:32,567 --> 00:19:36,633
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

416
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:57,300
Amazing!

417
00:19:57,433 --> 00:19:58,633
It is so relaxing here.

418
00:19:58,767 --> 00:20:00,633
It is beautiful!

419
00:20:00,767 --> 00:20:02,767
It really is beautiful.

420
00:20:02,933 --> 00:20:07,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:13,467
It is cold here.

422
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:17,367
Sir, a blanket,
in case you feel cold.

423
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:18,767
Thank you, Andrew.

424
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:20,200
Joey, here.

425
00:20:20,333 --> 00:20:21,200
You are cold.

426
00:20:21,333 --> 00:20:23,500
- Oh, thank you.
- I got you too.

427
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:26,467
Oh, thank you.

428
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,867
You really are Boss Idol.

429
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,267
That blanket is for me, okay?

430
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:30,633
Thank you.

431
00:20:30,767 --> 00:20:33,033
Get one for yourself inside.

432
00:20:33,167 --> 00:20:35,033
[CLEARS THROAT]

433
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,600
I am starting
to notice something.

434
00:20:36,733 --> 00:20:38,633
One more and we are moving.

435
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:44,300
Sir, I made hot chocolate
for you.

436
00:20:44,433 --> 00:20:46,767
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

437
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:48,467
Oh, Joey...

438
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,167
this is for you.

439
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:54,200
Not too hot, not too cold.

440
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:55,733
Just right.

441
00:20:57,033 --> 00:20:58,600
- [CLEARS THROAT]
- Thank you.

442
00:20:59,067 --> 00:21:00,467
Thank you.

443
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:06,300
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

444
00:21:10,467 --> 00:21:11,533
Ah...

445
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:12,833
Joey, my child...

446
00:21:12,967 --> 00:21:15,867
Oh, just a moment, okay?

447
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
I will talk to these three now.

448
00:21:18,967 --> 00:21:20,267
Follow me!

449
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:24,367
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

450
00:21:28,633 --> 00:21:30,100
Why?

451
00:21:30,233 --> 00:21:34,200
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:21:37,267 --> 00:21:41,467
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

453
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:46,667
You are blocking my way.

454
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:47,900
Where are you going now?

455
00:21:48,033 --> 00:21:50,433
If someone sees you,
this will be another problem.

456
00:21:50,567 --> 00:21:52,133
I am afraid that

457
00:21:52,267 --> 00:21:53,467
I might lose you.

458
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:55,100
Did enemies arrive?

459
00:21:55,233 --> 00:21:56,767
Yes, those three idiots.

460
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:58,467
You ruin every plan!

461
00:21:58,600 --> 00:21:59,500
You are a traitor, Oppa!

462
00:21:59,633 --> 00:22:01,167
What? Survival
of the fittest now?

463
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:03,700
If I had known, I would have
woken up earlier.

464
00:22:03,833 --> 00:22:04,800
- I wanted to say something.
- Good thing you are already...

465
00:22:04,933 --> 00:22:05,867
You go first.

466
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:06,867
I wish it could
always be like this.

467
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,500
Like we never have any problems.

468
00:22:08,633 --> 00:22:09,867
But we have one problem.

469
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,233
If she try anything,

470
00:22:11,367 --> 00:22:13,100
I will kill her myself.

471
00:22:13,233 --> 00:22:14,900
You are going to kill someone?
